title: "Corpus — Tier 9: the backends grammar"
type: document
---

# The backends grammar

The stateful blocks a phone app needs (0.33.0): a record with an owner and a
computed field, a list route, a tiered picker, a stepped flow, a model-bound
form, a derived value, a conditional section and a reminder.

::model[name=Entry owner=viewer]
- id: uuid pk
- core: enum(Joy,Trust) [required]
- level: range [min=1, max=10, labels="Barely felt it|All-consuming"]
- score: number = round(avg(level), 1)
::

::route[method=GET path=/_api/Entry returns=list(Entry) filter=date sort=date]
::

::flow[model=Entry]
:::step[title="Pick an emotion"]
::::picker[bind=entry.core tiers=2 emoji=false]
- Joy: Serenity · Joy | info="Content | Seeing a friend"
::::
:::
:::step[title="Why?" repeat=true]
- note: textarea [max=500, sentences=1..4, prompt="What caused it?"]
:::
::

::form[model=Entry]
- level: range [min=1, max=10, levels="2|4|7|9"]
::

::compute[name=daily_score expr="avg(entries.level)" source=/_api/Entry]
::

::when[bind=day.score op="<=" value=-8]
Reach out to someone you trust.
::

::schedule[bind=preference.reminder_time title="MoodMap" body="How are you feeling today?" link=/log]
::
